The first 32(0x0f - 0x1f) characters of the ASCII table are controls character.
pressing the ctrl-<character> will map the <character> to its control corresponding.

We are writing an escape sequence to the terminal. Escape sequences always start with an escape character '\x1b' (27) followed
by a [ character. Escape sequences instruct the terminal to do various text formatting tasks, such as coloring text,
moving the cursor around, and clearing parts of the screen.
